REPRO_EXACT [*] | Concrete input E1a (the printed-but-chosen case, V16's headline): pinned enumerable text paper_A.txt, line 412, prints "with β = 1/929.25 the ratio is 2.718" as its own result; the recipe producing the ratio is printed at line 410; β is printed → status PRINTED, origin CHOSEN (ORIG_CHOICE_STATED, verbatim quotation from line 411); all remaining inputs PRINTED. Under option (c), provenance does not bar consumption: §2 step 4 consumes every PRINTED/STANDARD record; the mechanical arithmetic yields the printed numeral at its printed precision. Concrete input E1b (stated-precision rounding): paper_B.txt, line 88, prints "the age is 13.8 Gyr"; recipe printed; H₀ = 67.36, Ω_m = 0.3153, Ω_Λ = 0.6847 printed verbatim and on C3's closed list → STANDARD; mechanical evaluation yields 13.797 Gyr; no precision stated for the claim, so "the reproduced value must round to the printed numeral at that precision" (§3) — 13.797 rounds to 13.8. | §1 (quantitative claim: a printed numeral the paper asserts as its own result) → §2 step 1 (extract number/units/equation, file and line) → §2 steps 2–3 (inputs listed; each PRINTED or STANDARD on the closed list) → §2 step 4 (mechanical attempt consuming exactly the PRINTED/STANDARD records) → §3 `REPRO_EXACT`: "the paper's number follows, within its own stated precision, from the paper's own recipe applied to the inputs it states (`PRINTED` or `STANDARD`). Report both numbers." No earlier precedence condition holds. The script computes `rests_on` beside it: E1a → USES_CHOSEN, E1b → DERIVED_ONLY. | reachable: YES

REPRO_FAILED [*] | Concrete input F1: paper_B.txt, line 91, prints "the age is 14.5 Gyr" as its own result of the same printed recipe, with the same printed closed-list inputs (H₀, Ω_m, Ω_Λ all STANDARD). The mechanical evaluation yields 13.797 Gyr, which does not round to 14.5 at the printed precision. Every input is PRINTED or STANDARD, so the recipe is fully determined by what the paper states. | §1 → §2 steps 1–4 (attempt completes; no BLOCKED/ABSENT input, no timeout) → §3 `REPRO_FAILED`: "the inputs the paper states are sufficient for its recipe, but the arithmetic does not give the paper's number. Report both numbers." Wording: "unreproduced from the stated inputs," not "error." `rests_on` reported beside it (here DERIVED_ONLY — a failure of arithmetic, not of provenance). | reachable: YES

REPRO_BLOCKED | Concrete input B1 (first limb): paper_C.txt, line 210, prints a result whose printed recipe needs a normalisation A; the paper does not print A's value but writes "using the value of Smith et al. (1999)" (line 211); Smith et al. (1999) is not an enumerable text pinned in R3C2_CORPUS_MANIFEST.md. Concrete input B2 (second limb): the named source IS an enumerable pinned text, but the value does not machine-match at its cited line — §2: "a cited value that does not machine-match at the named source's cited line, or whose named source is not an enumerable text of the manifest, files `REPRO_BLOCKED` under §3." | §2 step 3 → status BLOCKED ("traced to a named source but carrying no machine-matchable value"); recorded per C3 with origin IMPORTED, ORIG_CITATION evidence cited to the claiming paper's naming sentence, and no value → §2: "A seat may not supply a value for an `ABSENT` or `BLOCKED` input. Encountering one ends that claim's attempt." → §3 `REPRO_BLOCKED`: the paper "names a source (a citation) that either is not an enumerable text pinned in `R3C2_CORPUS_MANIFEST.md` or is an enumerable pinned text at whose cited line the value does not machine-match"; "whether that source is obtainable elsewhere is irrelevant, because the census may not open or consume it." Precedence: BLOCKED files before INPUT_ABSENT, NOT_EVALUABLE and the arithmetic group. | reachable: YES

REPRO_NOT_EVALUABLE | Concrete input N1 (timeout limb): paper_D.txt, line 77, prints a number whose printed recipe requires a stiff numerical integration; the attempt is launched through the committed wrapper as `/usr/bin/python3 r3c2_timeout.py 120.0 -- <command>` (§9); the deadline passes; the wrapper "prints `SYMBOLIC_TIMEOUT` and exits 124 — the reportable outcome" (§9). §3: "the arithmetic could not be completed within the 120-second cap." One repeat permitted (§4.2); on repeat timeout the filing stands. Concrete input N2 (machinery limb): the printed recipe requires a Boltzmann-solver run this lane does not have → "or requires machinery this lane does not have"; print `MACHINERY_UNAVAILABLE` (named at V15, §10.9) and the point reached. | §1 → §2 steps 1–4 (attempt begun; not terminable) → §3 `REPRO_NOT_EVALUABLE`: "Print `SYMBOLIC_TIMEOUT` when the 120-second cap is exceeded, or `MACHINERY_UNAVAILABLE` when the lane lacks the machinery, and the point reached." Precedence: after NO_DERIVATION_STATED/BLOCKED/INPUT_ABSENT, before the arithmetic group. | reachable: YES

REPRO_NO_DERIVATION_STATED | Concrete input ND1: paper_E.txt, line 55, prints "the transition redshift is z = 0.39" asserted as its own result; a full read of the paper finds no equation and no computational procedure that could produce it. §1 admits the candidate (a printed numeral asserted as the paper's own result; it is not attributed to another work). §2 step 1 finds nothing to extract; there is no recipe, so no inputs are listed and no ledger record exists. | §1 (claim included) → §2 step 1 (nothing to extract) → §3 `REPRO_NO_DERIVATION_STATED`: "the paper prints the claim as its own result but states no equation or computational procedure that could produce it, so there is nothing to attempt. Name the passage." Precedence: first — it files ahead of every other terminal condition. With no ledger record, §3 assigns `rests_on` `NOT_COMPUTED`, "and the `rests_on` tally reports a `NOT_COMPUTED` row." | reachable: YES

REPRO_INPUT_ABSENT | Concrete input A1: paper_F.txt, line 130, prints a result from a printed recipe that needs the present-day radiation density Ω_r; the paper neither prints Ω_r nor names any source for it — no citation sentence exists. | §2 step 3 → status ABSENT ("neither printed nor traced to any named source") → §2: "A seat may not supply a value for an `ABSENT`... input. Encountering one ends that claim's attempt." → §3 `REPRO_INPUT_ABSENT`: "an input the equation needs is `ABSENT` from the paper — neither printed nor traced to any named source — so the attempt stops there. Name the input." Boundaries exhibited, not assumed: had the paper named a source, B1/B2 applies and precedence files BLOCKED first; had the named source been a pinned enumerable text with a machine match at the cited line, the input would be PRINTED with origin IMPORTED (§2) and the claim attempted. | reachable: YES

Retired, not a row: `REPRO_AFTER_CHOICE` — carried in §3 only inside a note: "RETIRED at V10 by the principal's ruling adopting option (c)... it is retired, not repaired." Its former content now lives in the script-computed `rests_on` field (exhibited as USES_CHOSEN / USES_FITTED / USES_IMPORTED / USES_UNDECLARED in the supplementary table). It is not a declared per-claim outcome of V16, so C0 requires no row for it; the V9 unreachability finding (§10.3) concerned that retired class under the retired option-(b) definition and does not transfer to any V16 outcome.

