None. Every declared §3 outcome and every §4 class has a concrete exhibited input above. The rule applied is §5 C0: "An outcome for which no such input can be exhibited is UNREACHABLE, and this preregistration does not freeze until it is." No row triggered it. Accordingly: C0_REACHABILITY=PASS on line 2 (the second seat's independent verification is a separate artefact; this is the authoring seat's exhibition).

=====================================================================
SUPPLEMENTARY — DECLARED CONDITIONS THAT ARE NOT OUTCOMES
(Exhibited so the coverage check has a row for each. §3: "Candidate exclusions are not per-claim outcomes." The `rests_on` values are script-computed fields: "No seat writes `root_origins` or `rests_on`; the script rejects a ledger that arrives with either set.")
=====================================================================

Exclusion-ledger kinds (§3, five declared; §1 excludes these "by definition and not by taste"):
- EQUATION_NUMBER | paper_H.txt line 12 prints "...(4.7)" numbering an equation → §1 excluded kinds, "numerals that are equation numbers" → exclusion ledger, kind EQUATION_NUMBER | YES
- REFERENCE_NUMBER | "[13]" citation marker in running text → kind REFERENCE_NUMBER | YES
- PAGE_OR_LINE_NUMBER | "see p. 214" → kind PAGE_OR_LINE_NUMBER | YES
- DATE | "in 1998 the survey began" → kind DATE | YES
- ATTRIBUTED_NOT_DERIVED | "Planck reports Ω_m = 0.315" — a value "the paper attributes to another work without deriving" → kind ATTRIBUTED_NOT_DERIVED | YES

rests_on values (computed by the pinned script r3c2_ledger_tools.py from root origins; the master-only rule at §3: "`DERIVED_ONLY` when every root origin is `DERIVED`, `STANDARD` or `MEASURED`; otherwise the most severe root origin present, in the fixed order `USES_UNDECLARED` > `USES_IMPORTED` > `USES_FITTED` > `USES_CHOSEN`"):
- DERIVED_ONLY | E1b above: all roots DERIVED/STANDARD/MEASURED | YES
- USES_CHOSEN | E1a above: β printed with ORIG_CHOICE_STATED; no more severe root | YES
- USES_FITTED | an input whose cited sentence states a fit (ORIG_FIT_STATED); no UNDECLARED or IMPORTED root present | YES
- USES_IMPORTED | an input PRINTED-via-IMPORTED from a pinned enumerable text, machine-matched at its cited line (§2); no UNDECLARED root | YES
- USES_UNDECLARED | an input whose origin evidence is ORIG_SILENT with the seat's printed search (C3); most severe root | YES
- DISPUTED | the merged ledger carries `origin_alt` on an input in the claim's root set → "carries the pair computed under both classifications and is marked `DISPUTED`" (§3; C6: "the `rests_on` tally reports a `DISPUTED` row") | YES
- NOT_COMPUTED | ND1 above: no equation, no inputs, no ledger record → "a claim with no ledger record carries `rests_on` `NOT_COMPUTED`, and the `rests_on` tally reports a `NOT_COMPUTED` row" (§3) | YES

